    ],
    "searchCoverage": "Official Bluesky/AT Protocol authentication for this pinned edition is handle + app password exchanged via POST /xrpc/com.atproto.server.createSession for an accessJwt, then Authorization Bearer on subsequent XRPC calls. Applications with a user login flow should use OAuth instead. Native recipe auth cannot express that session minting or AT Protocol OAuth. Dated incident search on 2026-09-13 found DDoS availability events and credential-stuffed account takeovers, not a current unresolved Bluesky platform compromise.",
    "incidents": [
      {
        "date": "2026-04-17",
        "source": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/17/its-not-just-you-bluesky-is-sorta-down/",
        "finding": "Bluesky confirmed a sophisticated DDoS starting 2026-04-15 that disrupted feeds, notifications, threads, and search. The company said it had not seen evidence of unauthorized access to private data.",
        "limitation": "Historical availability incident. 2026-09-13 waiver keeps historical non-China incidents."
      },
      {
        "date": "2026-08-18",
        "source": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/18/bluesky-says-its-recent-outage-was-caused-by-another-ddos-attack/",
        "finding": "Bluesky confirmed a second DDoS of about 24 hours. Coverage distinguished this from data exfiltration.",
        "limitation": "Historical availability incident."
      },
      {
        "date": "2026-05-22",
        "source": "https://www.cybermaterial.com/p/russia-hacks-bluesky-accounts-to",
        "finding": "Researchers described compromised Bluesky user accounts used for influence posts. Bluesky safety later stated systems were not breached and individual accounts were compromised via credentials leaked elsewhere.",
        "limitation": "Account-credential stuffing, not a Bluesky platform API compromise."
      }
    ],
    "remainingGates": [
      "credentials: Bluesky app-password auth requires POST https://bsky.social/xrpc/com.atproto.server.createSession with identifier+password to mint accessJwt/refreshJwt; subsequent XRPC calls use Authorization Bearer accessJwt. Native http.auth cannot express login-then-bearer. Official apps should use AT Protocol OAuth, which also has no native oauth block for this shape.",
      "operationQuality: unsupported session minting. Pinned createBlueskySession cannot be expressed as a static Authorization header.",
      "live authentication unverified"
    ],
    "waiverAuthority": "User waiver dated 2026-09-13 permits historical non-China incident coverage."
  },
